# WRK-009 — build OUTPUTS must never enter the build context.
#
# Both images compile from source inside the image (control-plane:
# `RUN pnpm --filter ... build`; worker: `RUN tsc -p ...`), so a `dist/` from the
# developer's machine is never needed — and it is actively harmful: `COPY
# packages/worker-daemon/ packages/worker-daemon/` carried the local dist in, and
# `tsc` writes into that same directory WITHOUT removing outputs whose source has
# gone. A file deleted or moved in source therefore kept shipping in the image.
#
# That is exactly how the fabricating fake provider survived being moved out of
# the production source tree, and it is the same shape as the packages/db
# migrations bug: a stale artifact surviving a rebuild.
#
# It also shrinks the build context substantially (it was transferring ~400MB).
**/dist
